; join/race's faults (D220): an empty list, which has nothing to wait for;
; something that isn't a list; something in it that isn't a pid, found
; before it waits; the caller's own pid; and an actor, which can't be
; joined (D243). And a root racing processes that never end is a
; deadlock, which says which they are.

(defun kind (pid) (car (cadr (join pid))))
(pprint (kind (fork (join/race ()))))
(pprint (kind (fork (join/race 5))))
(pprint (kind (fork (join/race (list (fork (sleep 5)) 3)))))
(pprint (kind (fork (join/race (list $$)))))
(pprint (kind (fork (join/race (list (spawn (recv (_ :a))))))))
(join/race (list (fork (read (address))) (fork (read (address)))))
; warns: 9:32 10:32
